{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gentling-humanlike-tanager","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThree REB epic closeouts are blocked after all acceptance criteria were marked complete and their open children were closed:\n\n- `nauseating-inquiring-ibex` / `95da-0b4f-06a8-4b9c`\n- `subjective-sudden-goitered` / `df55-1305-956e-431b`\n- `decorous-plucky-wrasse` / `e867-0f39-b887-40fa`\n\nEach close fails before the completion verifier with:\n\n```text\nError: cannot close <epic>: it records file_impact (a code change) but no commit references it (nor any of its descendants). Add a 'rebar-ticket: <id>' trailer to the commit that implements it, then retry (or override with --force=\"<reason>\"). Completion verification cannot confirm the work landed without a referencing commit.\n```\n\nPrior bug `ferric-jet-scorpion` (`1edf-2261-a092-43e5`) fixed the simpler case where a parent should credit commits from its transitive descendants. This bug tracks the remaining closeout failure: coordination/rollup epics may be proven by closed children, administrative duplicate/obsolete dispositions, and replacement tickets, yet the deterministic precheck still prevents a non-force close.\n\n## RCA Plan\n\n1. Reproduce using the three blocked epics above and capture the full close-precheck error.\n2. Locate the deterministic completion precheck and referencing-commit scan in `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` and its tests.\n3. Trace the accepted-id set built for an epic: own id, transitive descendants, and any replacement/superseding tickets recorded by administrative close dispositions.\n4. Determine whether the failure is a defect or intended policy. If it is intended behavior requiring policy change, stop and escalate. If it is a defect, fix only the missing evidence path while preserving the fail-closed protection for code tickets with no landed/referenced work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The bug is classified with RCA as either a genuine defect or intended policy; the ticket records the exact code path and evidence.\n- [ ] If defect, a RED test reproduces a blocked epic close where closed child/replacement evidence should satisfy the deterministic landed-work precheck.\n- [ ] The fix preserves the current protection: a code-impact ticket with no referencing commit in its accepted evidence set still fails with `cannot confirm the work landed`.\n- [ ] The three known blocked epics (`ibex`, `goitered`, `wrasse`) can close without `--force` after the fix lands, or the ticket records why a policy decision is required instead.\n- [ ] Targeted tests and `make verify` pass before Gerrit upload.\n","id":"9181-7c2e-5718-4f7f","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion close precheck still misses implemented descendant/replacement evidence for epic closeouts"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788895094276895001,"uuid":"8582ff6e-7791-49de-ab33-68915ccb5a02"}